# Content Curator

`Content Curator` is a two-phase personal curation system for OpenClaw + Obsidian:

1. deterministic article discovery/extraction and file-backed storage;
2. semantic curation by the isolated OpenClaw agent `curator`, followed by one atomic Markdown publication to Obsidian.

The ingest layer never uses an LLM as a crawler and never performs open web search. Each source is constrained to its configured landing page, RSS/Atom feed, or explicitly allowlisted sitemap.

## Scope

Current version processes **web articles only**. `telegram` and `podcast` sources are valid configuration entries but are deliberately ignored by article ingest. Article source count is calculated dynamically from `sources.yaml`.

## Architecture

```text
sources.yaml
   │
   ▼
discovery ──► date filtering ──► detail fetch ──► extraction
   │                                      │
   │                                      ├─ HTTP first
   │                                      └─ Chromium fallback
   ▼
data/runs/YYYY-MM-DD/article_ingest.json
+ data/content/YYYY-MM/*.txt
   │
   ▼
OpenClaw skill: content-curator
   │
   ├─ metadata/excerpt triage
   ├─ full text only for potentially useful items
   ├─ one analysis per unique content_id
   └─ finalize-day completeness gate
   │
   ▼
Obsidian: YYYY-MM-DD.md
```

Storage is JSON / JSONL / TXT / Markdown only; there is no application database.

## Install locally

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e '.[browser,dev]'
playwright install chromium
pytest -q
ruff check curator tests
git diff --check
```

## CLI

All commands return valid JSON on stdout.

```bash
curator article-sources --config sources.yaml
curator discover-articles --date 2026-09-18 --tz Europe/Moscow --sources anthropic_news --workers 2 --config sources.yaml
curator ingest-articles --date 2026-09-18 --tz Europe/Moscow --sources anthropic_news --stateless --workers 2 --config sources.yaml
curator list-ingest --date 2026-09-18 --config sources.yaml
curator read-content 'article:...' --config sources.yaml
curator list-analysis --date 2026-09-18 --config sources.yaml
curator save-analysis 'article:...' --date 2026-09-18 --category summary_enough --score 8 --reason 'Useful' --summary '...' --topics 'agents,evals' --config sources.yaml
curator finalize-day --date 2026-09-18 --config sources.yaml
curator publish-digest --date 2026-09-18 --input /path/to/digest.md --config sources.yaml
curator stats --from 2026-09-01 --to 2026-09-30 --chart /tmp/curator-stats.png --config sources.yaml
curator cleanup --config sources.yaml
```

Production ingest is stateful. Historical `--stateless` runs never update state and reject undated index/feed candidates instead of rescuing them with a detail-page date. Re-ingesting a selected source replaces only that source's slice in the stored cumulative daily manifest; stdout for the invocation contains only requested sources.

## Data layout

```text
data/
  runs/YYYY-MM-DD/
    article_ingest.json
    discoveries.jsonl
    extraction.jsonl
    analysis.jsonl
    finalized.json
  content/YYYY-MM/
    <hash>.json
    <hash>.txt
  history/YYYY-MM.jsonl
  state/
  raw/
```

The final digest is never stored as `data/runs/YYYY-MM-DD/digest.md`.

## Obsidian

```dotenv
CURATOR_DATA_DIR=/opt/content-curator/data
OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH=/home/dtadmin/obsidian-vault
OBSIDIAN_DIGEST_DIR="Digital Twin/90 Agent/Content Curator/Digests"
```

`publish-digest` requires complete analysis, re-finalizes history idempotently, validates the date, blocks traversal outside the vault, and atomically writes only:

```text
/home/dtadmin/obsidian-vault/Digital Twin/90 Agent/Content Curator/Digests/YYYY-MM-DD.md
```

## OpenClaw

The repository includes `skill/SKILL.md`. Install it into the dedicated `curator` agent:

```bash
openclaw skills install /opt/content-curator/skill \
  --as content-curator \
  --agent curator \
  --force
```

Full VPS setup, security, manual verification, and daily automation are in [`docs/VPS_SETUP.md`](docs/VPS_SETUP.md). Live historical publisher checks are in [`docs/ACCEPTANCE.md`](docs/ACCEPTANCE.md).

## Security

Article bodies are untrusted input. The skill forbids executing instructions embedded in content. Keep `curator` sandboxed, route exec explicitly to the Gateway, and allowlist only `/opt/content-curator/.venv/bin/curator`. Do not enable global yolo/full access.
